# Clean decision docs

> Install this rule **per consumer project** (`.cursor/rules/`). Full policy: skill `clean-decision-docs`.

When you **write or revise** a tech spec, design doc, or implementation plan (including after critic findings or human `revise`):

1. Load and follow skill **`clean-decision-docs`**.
2. Rewrite the file as **current truth only** — as if today's decisions were always the decisions.
3. Put "what I changed this turn" in **chat**, never as a Changelog / What-changed / Before-After section inside the file.
4. Forbidden in the file body: "fixed", "changed to", "was previously", "after critique", "per F\<id\>", strikethrough of old draft text, dual old+new wording.
5. Allowed: tech-spec **Rejected alternatives** as one-line *current* rationale; rollout steps that name temporary *system* states; Status `draft` / `approved` / `skip`.

Does not apply to pure Q&A, critic *reports* (those are allowed to narrate findings), or code comments (see `code-comments`).
